+
+#### [ContextGem](https://github.com/shcherbak-ai/contextgem)
+> **Description:** ContextGem is designed for structured extraction from documents with LLMs and is directly relevant to legal review and contract analysis. The README emphasizes automated prompt generation, automatic data modeling and validators, paragraph and sentence reference mapping, justifications for extracted answers, multilingual support, and a reusable extraction pipeline. GitHub shows 1.8k stars, Python as the primary language, and an Apache-2.0 license. The latest GitHub release is dated March 16, 2026. For lawyers building issue lists, obligation summaries, or clause extraction from long agreements, it offers a faster route than wiring together a generic LLM stack by hand.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/shcherbak-ai/contextgem](https://github.com/shcherbak-ai/contextgem)
+- **Stars:** 1.8k ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
