+#### [Blackstone](https://github.com/ICLRandD/Blackstone)
+> **Description:** Blackstone is a spaCy-based pipeline and model for long-form legal text, especially case law and other common law materials. The README emphasizes that it was trained for common-law entities and concepts, ships with custom legal sentence segmentation, and includes helpers for compound case references and legislation linking. GitHub shows 680 stars, Python as the primary language, and an Apache-2.0 license. The `legaltech` topic page lists the repository as updated on July 16, 2024. For lawyers working with judgments, pleadings, or research corpora, it is one of the clearest open legal-NLP building blocks.
