+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for lawyers in 2026?
+For legal-native work, start with `LexNLP`, `Blackstone`, `CourtListener`, `eyecite`, `DocuSeal`, and `ContextGem`. For the broader self-hosted stack lawyers actually need, add `Docling`, `OCRmyPDF`, `Presidio`, `Qdrant`, `Haystack`, and `AnythingLLM`.
+
+### Are these AI tools actually open source and on GitHub?
+Yes. Every item in this list points to a public `github.com` repository. Closed SaaS products, marketing pages without source code, and non-GitHub downloads were intentionally excluded.
+
+### Which open source AI tools help with contract review for lawyers?
+The most relevant repositories here are `ContextGem`, `LexNLP`, `ContraxSuite`, `LawBotics`, `Template Archive`, `DocuSeal`, and `OpenSign`. They cover clause extraction, contract templates, document review, and signing workflows.
+
+### What is the best open source OCR stack for legal PDFs?
+`OCRmyPDF` is the clearest OCR-first answer for scanned legal PDFs. `Docling` and `Unstructured` are stronger if you also need layout-aware parsing, export to structured formats, or downstream RAG ingestion.
+
+### Which tools are safest for confidential legal documents?
+For privacy-sensitive workflows, prioritize self-hosted repos with local execution options such as `Docling`, `OCRmyPDF`, `Presidio`, `Qdrant`, `AnythingLLM`, and `Haystack`. `Presidio` is the standout choice for masking or redacting PII before further processing.
+
+### Can a law firm build a private legal ChatGPT with open source tools?
+Yes. A typical stack would be `Docling` or `Unstructured` for ingestion, `Presidio` for redaction, `Qdrant` for retrieval, and either `AnythingLLM`, `Flowise`, `Haystack`, or `LangChain` for the assistant layer.
+
+### Are there enough legal-specific open source repos, or is this still a gap?
+It is still a gap. Legal-native open source is much smaller than the broader self-hosted AI ecosystem, so the strongest practical stacks usually combine a handful of legal-specific repos with general-purpose open infrastructure for OCR, RAG, privacy, and workflow orchestration.
+
